                                "sense_id": "4080ae18-7791-3428-a9e2-df71276d39ae",
                                "text": "[…] You speak like a green girl,\nUnsifted in such perilous circumstance."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "56fb3f9d-98ed-47c2-8503-038cd88e6c46",
                                "sense_id": "4080ae18-7791-3428-a9e2-df71276d39ae",
                                "text": "1765, George Colman, The Comedies of Terence, Translated into Familiar Blank Verse, London: T. Becket & P. A. De Hondt, 2nd edition, 1768, Volume I, Preface, p. xxxii,\nBut each man’s understanding, such as it is, must be his guide; and he, who has not courage to make a free use of it, but obtrudes the opinions of others, unsifted and unexamined, on his readers, betrays more want of respect for their understanding, than diffidence of his own."
                            }
